# curl -- libcurl, which appstream links to fetch catalogue metadata.
#
# Packaged for that rather than for the command-line tool, though the tool comes
# with it and is worth having on a live ISO.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://curl.se/download/curl-8.13.0.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=4a093979a3c2d02de2fbc00549a32771007f2e78032c6faa5ecd2f7a9e152025
SRC_DIR=curl-8.13.0

# --without-ssl, and this is the second package in the set forced into it.
#
# curl 8.13 does not compile against OpenSSL 4.0:
#
#   lib/vtls/openssl.c:614: error: invalid use of incomplete typedef
#                           'ASN1_BIT_STRING'
#
# which is the same wall Python 3.13's _ssl hit -- OpenSSL 4.0 made the ASN1_*
# string types opaque, and both projects reach directly into them. Two
# independent consumers failing the same way is a fact about the OpenSSL
# version this distribution pins, not about either of them.
#
# So libcurl is built with no TLS backend at all. What that costs, stated
# plainly: this libcurl cannot fetch an https URL. It is packaged for
# appstream, which links it to download catalogue metadata -- a path nothing on
# a live ISO takes, since libadwaita only ever asks appstream to parse local
# metainfo. The command-line tool ships too and is similarly http-only.
#
# The real fix is a distribution-level decision between a newer curl, an older
# OpenSSL, or packaging GnuTLS and building curl against that. rust already
# depends on OpenSSL 4, so it is not a decision this recipe can make.
#
# --enable-threaded-resolver: the alternative is a resolver that blocks the
# whole process on DNS, which in a GUI is a frozen window.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --without-ssl \
--enable-threaded-resolver --without-libpsl --disable-ldap --disable-ldaps"
